{
  "schema": 1,
  "note": "TWO-LAYER cross-language golden fixture (m20e AM4). Layer 1 (Rust, observability_tests.rs): for every case whose expected_module_json is NOT null, build_log_line(evt, extra_fields_json, Breadcrumb{cause, sched, phase}) must equal expected_module_json BYTE-FOR-BYTE; cases whose expected_module_json is null are JS-only (forged or non-module lines) and the Rust mirror SKIPS them. Layer 2 (JS, parse.test.mjs): parseHostLine(host_line) must produce exactly the expect_* fields, and for the module cases its payloadText must equal expected_module_json byte-for-byte. host_line is the HOST envelope (shape: ops/observability/alloy/config.alloy lines 31-40) whose message string carries the module payload re-escaped. Neither consumer ever tests the other layer. The Rust mirror calls build_log_line DIRECTLY, never mr_log_breadcrumb: the nested-evt-object case deliberately carries a reserved key inside extra_fields_json, which mr_log_breadcrumb debug_asserts against (that assert is compiled out of release wasm, which is precisely why the relay must defend against it). ts values are host-stamped microsecond DIGIT STRINGS and are realistic 16-digit magnitudes except ts-short and ts-precision, which are deliberate ordering/precision probes.",
